    "summary": "Alabama shows widespread resistance, with 43 moratoria and nearly every county scored high for being blocked; standouts are Coffee, Baldwin, Walker, Morgan and Elmore (scores 0.90-0.93), where commissions unanimously adopted moratoria of roughly six to twelve months citing water, noise and land concerns. Organized pushback is visible in Morgan (Say No to Data Centers petition), Talladega (Save The Creek, 685 signatures), Hale and Marengo (Gallion petitions and forums), Escambia (about 400 signatures against a 2,700-acre project), and Lowndes, where residents sued over the $33.1B Project Red Clay. Resistance is not uniform: Tuscaloosa is the only county scored as approved, Chilton rescinded its moratorium after the chair said state law gives the county no authority to deny data centers, and many high scores are predicted from neighboring counties with no local sources."
