    "summary": "Texas shows widespread resistance concentrated in moratorium and pause actions: Austin, Cass, Martin and Stephens counties adopted or approved moratoria, and Hays County passed a 180-day water protection pause after San Marcos banned data centers. Strong opposition also appears in Brazoria and Archer, where commissioners denied tax abatements, and in Henderson County, where a petition led the developer to withdraw a 700-acre project. Resistance is weaker in counties such as Deaf Smith, Nolan, Scurry, Shackelford and Taylor, which approved abatements despite scattered resident objections, and many counties are rated high only by neighbor-based prediction with no local sources."
